een and behind the leaf-base blocks the trunk carries coarse brown fibrous matting and loose strands of sheath fibre, filling the gaps of the lattice with a shaggy texture.", "reference_ids": ["reference-1", "reference-2"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "T-TRUNK-SINGLE-COLUMN", "priority": "core", "observation": "Single unbranched columnar stem of roughly constant diameter carrying the crown at its apex; no branching visible in any view.", "reference_ids": ["reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "T-CROWN-HEMISPHERE", "priority": "core", "observation": "Crown is a dense, roughly hemispherical to shuttlecock-shaped mass of many dozens of fronds, widest well above the trunk apex, with the newest erect spear-like fronds at the centre and progressively lower-angled older fronds outward.", "reference_ids": ["reference-0", "reference-1"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "T-FRUIT-CLUSTERS", "priority": "secondary", "observation": "In reference-0, pendulous fruiting structures hang from the crown centre: stout pale-orange stalks branching into dense strands bearing many small orange-to-red ovoid fruits, at least two or three such clusters visible. No fruit or flower structures are visible in reference-1 or reference-2.", "reference_ids": ["reference-0"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "T-DEAD-FROND-SKIRT", "priority": "secondary", "observation": "A skirt of dead, brown, collapsed fronds hangs beneath the living crown in reference-0, draping against the upper trunk. Reference-1 shows dry brown lower fronds and fibrous sheath remnants at the crown base but no long hanging skirt.", "reference_ids": ["reference-0", "reference-1"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "T-PETIOLE-SHEATH-COLLAR", "priority": "secondary", "observation": "At the crown base the frond bases are broad, flattened and overlapping, pale green to straw and reddish-brown, forming a collar of sheathing material around the apical bud; reddish-brown fibrous and orange-tinged tissue is visible b